  "schema": 1,
  "title": "which parts of a turn need a Unix shell, and what it costs to stop needing one",
  "source": "code-read",
  "source_detail": "protocol/lanes.md:29-40 and protocol/graphs.md:415-423, :447, :461-463, :535 — every command an agent retypes on an ordinary turn; Q1 of this plan",
  "explanation": "Neither underlying tool needs a shell — Codex and the viewer are both single commands. The shell is entirely in [the wrapping](#the-wrapping), and the two boxes below it say why that wrapping is there rather than being laziness: one recovers the handle that makes a lane resumable, the other works around a server that sometimes returns and sometimes does not. Any option that deletes the wrapping has to answer both. Leaves out the install-time scripts, which stay shell under a decision already taken.",
  "groups": [
